cff-version: 1.2.1
title: "iot-bench-deploy: replica-scalable fixed-resource deploys and open-model benchmarking of FIWARE, EdgeX and ThingsBoard"
message: >-
  Benchmark tooling with exploratory (not campaign) qualification for three
  self-hosted IoT platforms behind HAProxy on fixed-core, fixed-memory
  budgets, plus an open-model (constant-arrival) k6 generator with
  identity-based reconciliation gates.
type: software
authors:
  - name: "IoT benchmark project (owner of record pending — see SECURITY.md)"
version: "0.1.0-dev"
date-released: "2026-10-29"
license: "UNLICENSED"  # owner decision pending; see docs/status.md §7
repository-code: "https://example.invalid/iot-bench-deploy"
abstract: >-
  One Docker Compose stack per IoT platform, identical shape
  (HAProxy -> replicated tier(s) -> single stateful tier), scaling only the
  replica count N within fixed per-instance memory and shared-core pools;
  k6-based open-model load generation; per-run manifests, resource guards
  and identity-based store reconciliation.
keywords:
  - iot
  - benchmark
  - fiware
  - edgex
  - thingsboard
  - k6
  - reproducibility
